WEBVTT

00:03.980 --> 00:05.230
Part the First

00:48.310 --> 00:50.020
Mr. Medicine Seller,

00:52.490 --> 00:55.320
we don’t want none.

00:56.820 --> 01:01.580
You’ll scare off the customers, standing there like that.

01:01.580 --> 01:05.160
I’ll have to ask you to leave.

01:10.590 --> 01:13.170
No, no.

01:13.590 --> 01:15.130
I’d like a room

01:15.760 --> 01:17.760
for the night.

01:18.550 --> 01:21.220
Yes, please.

01:21.220 --> 01:22.890
Yes, please.

01:27.560 --> 01:28.900
Oh my.

01:30.650 --> 01:32.980
Long time no see

01:57.430 --> 02:01.760
The blue moon illuminated

02:01.800 --> 02:05.730
your wandering shadow.

02:06.350 --> 02:10.230
I could never tell you all I wanted to say.

02:10.230 --> 02:15.150
It was so very frustrating.

02:15.230 --> 02:19.030
I think about your faked smile,

02:19.610 --> 02:23.660
and forget all the hot tears we shed.

02:24.120 --> 02:26.330
What do these empty husks,

02:26.370 --> 02:32.170
those empty eyes of yours, reflect, my dear?

02:32.920 --> 02:37.380
The transient quarter moon

02:37.760 --> 02:39.550
hides in a rift in the clouds,

02:39.510 --> 02:41.930
as darkness seeps up from the ground.

02:41.970 --> 02:46.390
Tell me the truth, please.

02:46.720 --> 02:48.560
Are you so despondent

02:48.640 --> 02:53.020
that you still sit alone, sighing?

02:53.690 --> 02:55.150
That Night

03:03.030 --> 03:07.120
It’s awfully cold, isn’t it?

03:07.750 --> 03:09.410
I’m sorry.

03:11.620 --> 03:13.750
But it’s bitter, isn’t it?

03:14.170 --> 03:16.670
Well, it is from China.

03:17.050 --> 03:19.800
Do you have anything else?

03:21.340 --> 03:24.680
Do you own this inn, ma’am?

03:24.680 --> 03:26.350
Yes indeed.

03:26.970 --> 03:31.310
I’ve had the building itself since I was a girl.

03:36.610 --> 03:38.780
What was it

03:40.570 --> 03:42.910
before you made it an inn?

03:42.910 --> 03:45.620
Hmm, what was it?

03:45.950 --> 03:47.830
I forget.

03:47.830 --> 03:49.910
Guess I’m getting old.

03:54.420 --> 03:55.960
Excuse me!

03:58.630 --> 04:02.930
Do you have a room for the night?

04:05.470 --> 04:09.100
Sorry, but we’re full up.

04:09.520 --> 04:11.020
Look somewhere else.

04:11.020 --> 04:13.850
You’re the only ones open!

04:13.850 --> 04:15.440
There’re no vacancies.

04:15.440 --> 04:16.190
I’ve got plenty of money!

04:16.900 --> 04:18.320
You can even have my umbrella!

04:18.320 --> 04:18.980
Could it be?

04:18.980 --> 04:20.440
That’s right.

04:20.440 --> 04:22.030
You took the last vacancy.

04:21.400 --> 04:22.030
Please!

04:22.030 --> 04:22.610
Please!

04:22.610 --> 04:25.200
Well, what about this one?

04:25.200 --> 04:28.830
Actually, I’m being chased.

04:28.830 --> 04:31.080
If they find me,

04:31.080 --> 04:32.620
I’ll be killed for sure!

04:32.620 --> 04:36.750
Ooh! That’s quite the story.

04:41.920 --> 04:43.050
Oh.

04:44.510 --> 04:46.140
It’s true.

04:50.140 --> 04:52.140
Well, it’s raining pretty hard.

04:52.480 --> 05:03.650
We wouldn’t ordinarily turn such a
nice young lady as yourself away, but…

04:53.810 --> 04:54.600
It stinks.

04:59.570 --> 05:01.400
It’s another Chinese remedy.

05:01.400 --> 05:05.570
They call it Hansuke lotion.

05:06.570 --> 05:08.240
You see?

05:10.120 --> 05:15.250
If I stand in the rain any longer, my child

05:17.580 --> 05:19.840
will surely die!

05:28.340 --> 05:30.930
Are you pregnant?

05:32.140 --> 05:37.730
Goodness, I can’t believe you!

05:37.730 --> 05:39.360
Mistress!

05:39.360 --> 05:43.190
Tokuji, why aren’t you just kicking her out?

05:44.860 --> 05:49.160
I’m sorry, but we don’t want any trouble.

05:49.160 --> 05:51.030
Get out of here!

05:51.030 --> 05:52.700
If I do…

05:55.040 --> 05:57.620
If I do leave, by tomorrow morning

06:00.960 --> 06:06.220
my corpse and that of my infant
child will be lying in your doorway.

06:07.760 --> 06:11.350
Don’t you think that would get you in a good deal of trouble?

06:11.350 --> 06:12.810
I don’t take kindly to threats.

06:14.100 --> 06:17.230
It isn’t a threat!

06:17.600 --> 06:21.190
I want to raise a healthy child!

06:21.730 --> 06:24.730
If I stay outside, I won’t be able to protect him!

06:24.730 --> 06:26.070
Tokuji,

06:26.070 --> 06:27.150
a word.

06:26.490 --> 06:27.150
Please!

06:27.150 --> 06:28.360
Sure.

06:28.360 --> 06:29.780
Please!

06:29.780 --> 06:32.410
Please! Please!

06:30.160 --> 06:32.410
Take her upstairs.

06:32.410 --> 06:34.160
Take her upstairs.

06:34.160 --> 06:35.160
Wha—!?

06:35.160 --> 06:37.160
That room?

06:43.920 --> 06:46.260
It can’t be helped.

06:47.720 --> 06:52.680
I’ll take her there, you get a bed ready.

06:53.890 --> 06:54.970
All right.

06:55.890 --> 06:58.770
Um, I…

07:00.600 --> 07:02.940
I am in your debt.

07:15.700 --> 07:16.410
There we go.

07:21.670 --> 07:25.460
She could have stayed in my room.

07:36.310 --> 07:41.480
We don’t usually let customers in
this room, so keep this to yourself.

07:41.480 --> 07:44.400
Just try not to cause any trouble.

07:44.400 --> 07:45.020
I will.

07:48.440 --> 07:50.900
Um, ma’am?

07:50.900 --> 07:52.740
What now?

07:52.740 --> 07:56.740
I don’t care what it is, but I’d like something to eat.

08:04.080 --> 08:07.250
I wonder who did this.

08:07.250 --> 08:11.010
Well, I’ll have Tokuji take care of it in the morning.

08:13.340 --> 08:16.140
I couldn’t make much more than a bit of rice.

08:16.140 --> 08:17.100
That’s just fine.

08:38.450 --> 08:40.080
What are you doing?

08:42.500 --> 08:46.170
They’re up awfully late.

08:46.170 --> 08:51.920
You’ll be able to eat all you like, soon.

08:51.920 --> 08:54.590
You really want this child, don’t you?

08:54.590 --> 08:55.680
I do.

08:55.680 --> 09:00.970
I’m obviously not privy to all the
details, but can you really raise it on your own?

09:00.970 --> 09:02.180
I intend to.

09:02.180 --> 09:03.980
Ah, do you now?

09:03.980 --> 09:08.310
Well, at least you’re young.

09:08.310 --> 09:10.230
Seems a bit naive, though.

09:10.230 --> 09:14.030
You don’t even have a steady supply of food.

09:14.570 --> 09:18.820
Are you sure you’re not giving birth simply out of spite?

09:19.200 --> 09:22.450
Do you think it would be happy with no-one to care for it?

09:29.790 --> 09:31.130
I…

09:34.090 --> 09:37.050
I want him to live.

09:40.220 --> 09:45.310
What a strange woman. So strong-willed, almost to a fault.

09:48.730 --> 09:54.440
I was never able to do anything as irresponsible as that.

09:50.690 --> 09:52.690
Ma’am?

10:12.380 --> 10:14.800
So warm.

10:14.800 --> 10:17.260
Your bed will be here shortly.

10:17.260 --> 10:18.970
Oh, right.

10:18.970 --> 10:21.970
I have to make you some food, too.

10:27.270 --> 10:31.770
Thank you so much.

10:44.910 --> 10:46.120
A doll?

10:53.670 --> 10:56.880
Hey there, Medicine Seller, what’s the matter?

10:57.510 --> 11:01.550
I was heading to the lavatory.

11:01.550 --> 11:03.430
I got a little lost.

11:03.430 --> 11:05.140
Oh, well then.

11:05.140 --> 11:07.310
It’s just at the end of that hall.

11:13.110 --> 11:14.730
Thank you.

11:19.030 --> 11:21.150
Are there any rooms above here?

11:21.150 --> 11:25.370
None at all. It’s just a storeroom.

11:25.370 --> 11:27.120
I would ask you not to go up.

11:31.080 --> 11:32.960
I see.

11:32.960 --> 11:35.290
Oh, I should pay for those medicines.

11:36.800 --> 11:39.170
No,

11:39.170 --> 11:41.470
tomorrow will be fine.

11:44.680 --> 11:46.100
Good night to you.

11:52.020 --> 11:56.270
Where did I drop my charm?

12:00.320 --> 12:01.820
Give that back!

12:12.210 --> 12:13.710
Where did you…

12:13.710 --> 12:14.880
Give it back!

12:15.880 --> 12:17.920
Give it back!

12:17.920 --> 12:20.170
Give it back!

12:20.170 --> 12:21.550
Give it back!

12:25.300 --> 12:26.600
Is it yours?

12:27.350 --> 12:28.350
Yup.

12:32.310 --> 12:34.140
I’m so sorry.

12:34.140 --> 12:36.400
Here you are.

12:38.320 --> 12:39.730
Are you pregnant?

12:40.070 --> 12:42.650
I am.

12:42.650 --> 12:47.820
It shouldn’t be more than four months or so now.

12:47.820 --> 12:49.330
Are you happy?

12:49.330 --> 12:51.040
Yes, of course.

12:51.410 --> 12:53.870
Hey, let’s go over there.

12:53.870 --> 12:55.250
I’m afraid not.

12:55.250 --> 12:58.420
You should get back to your own roo—

13:14.140 --> 13:15.640
So cold.

13:54.850 --> 13:57.310
I will not return home!

13:57.310 --> 13:59.060
Leave me be!

13:59.060 --> 14:03.070
Do not give birth to this child.

14:03.070 --> 14:06.530
If it were to come back and claim its birthright,

14:06.530 --> 14:10.910
it would be quite an inconvenience to the master and mistress.

14:10.910 --> 14:13.790
I’ve cut myself off from the young master!

14:13.790 --> 14:19.290
That ignorant little fool does not concern me.

14:20.920 --> 14:23.590
I just want to give birth!

14:25.420 --> 14:27.260
That’s all!

14:39.350 --> 14:42.520
I can’t return empty-handed, having come all this way.

14:42.520 --> 14:43.820
Don’t kill me!

14:44.570 --> 14:46.990
No! Please!

14:46.990 --> 14:47.900
My son!

14:47.900 --> 14:48.360
Ready to die?

14:49.030 --> 14:49.860
My son!

14:49.860 --> 14:50.490
Prepare to die.

14:50.490 --> 14:53.030
Think of my son!

15:47.050 --> 15:48.260
There it is.

16:07.190 --> 16:10.320
Just what is going on here?

16:11.700 --> 16:14.410
What is this?

16:12.610 --> 16:14.410
What are you doing here?

16:14.410 --> 16:15.870
Did you do this?

16:17.740 --> 16:19.040
Of course not.

16:19.450 --> 16:23.670
Oh no! It’s all because you let her stay in this room!

16:19.450 --> 16:21.290
It protected her?

16:21.290 --> 16:23.670
But why?

16:23.670 --> 16:24.420
Tokuji!

16:24.420 --> 16:27.590
Go run to the castle.

16:27.590 --> 16:31.170
That will not be necessary.

16:31.170 --> 16:33.300
Of course it’s necessary!

16:33.300 --> 16:35.640
Only a criminal would object to calling the authorities!

16:35.640 --> 16:37.600
You must have done it!

16:36.140 --> 16:37.600
He didn’t!

16:38.260 --> 16:40.680
I saw it.

16:40.680 --> 16:43.640
He was not the culprit.

16:45.440 --> 16:46.690
Oh?

16:47.980 --> 16:49.020
What, then,

16:50.690 --> 16:52.110
did you see?

16:56.450 --> 16:59.450
He was caught, and pulled up.

16:59.450 --> 17:01.660
Then spun around.

17:01.660 --> 17:04.500
Around and around and around and around.

17:04.500 --> 17:07.380
Oh?

17:07.380 --> 17:10.880
Around and around and around and around?

17:13.130 --> 17:14.930
Medicine Seller?

17:14.930 --> 17:17.680
Just who are you?

17:17.680 --> 17:20.680
What are you doing in this room, anyway?

17:21.220 --> 17:26.190
The culprit was not human.

17:29.230 --> 17:30.610
It opened by itself.

17:33.740 --> 17:35.570
What is that?

17:36.660 --> 17:42.080
Wh—Why would a medicine seller
be carrying such a ridiculous sword?

17:42.080 --> 17:45.540
I came to kill.

17:47.290 --> 17:49.920
K—Kill what?

17:56.380 --> 17:59.970
The Mononoke, of course.

18:00.390 --> 18:02.970
Something must have killed him.

18:03.470 --> 18:06.430
Don’t be stupid!

18:06.430 --> 18:08.350
As you can see, though,

18:08.350 --> 18:10.110
he was indeed killed.

18:10.110 --> 18:11.650
Could any man do this?

18:11.650 --> 18:12.900
Well of course—

18:12.900 --> 18:13.440
Not.

18:14.150 --> 18:15.740
There, there.

18:16.950 --> 18:18.200
What a terrible smell.

18:18.200 --> 18:20.870
What is that doing here?

18:22.660 --> 18:24.290
Where did it come from?

18:24.290 --> 18:26.200
It was here from the beginning.

18:26.790 --> 18:28.080
A child came to get it.

18:28.080 --> 18:29.290
A child?

18:29.290 --> 18:31.130
There must be some here.

18:31.130 --> 18:33.090
What are you talking about?

18:33.090 --> 18:36.720
None of tonight’s customers had children with them.

18:36.720 --> 18:40.680
Th—Then, what were those footsteps, and children’s voices?

18:41.220 --> 18:44.220
You must have heard them when we were walking up here.

18:44.220 --> 18:45.390
No, I didn’t.

18:45.390 --> 18:46.930
Huh?

18:48.980 --> 18:49.890
There!

18:49.890 --> 18:52.770
There’s a group of children right over there!

18:59.360 --> 19:01.320
What now?

19:02.870 --> 19:05.660
Over there, too!

19:10.790 --> 19:11.540
Huh?

19:15.050 --> 19:16.210
And above us!

19:16.210 --> 19:19.510
What do you mean? This is the top floor!

19:19.510 --> 19:20.430
The body…

19:21.180 --> 19:22.010
It’s gone.

19:23.430 --> 19:25.430
They’re coming from right over there!

19:27.020 --> 19:28.100
And from there!

19:34.480 --> 19:36.190
That’s as far as you’ll come!

20:05.220 --> 20:10.020
There are Mononoke here that are bound to this inn.

20:10.020 --> 20:13.730
Children, babies’ cries, and

20:14.980 --> 20:16.520
birth water?

20:16.520 --> 20:19.230
This is a Zashikiwarashi.

20:21.110 --> 20:24.570
Certain conditions must be met for
the Sword of Exorcism to be drawn.

20:24.570 --> 20:29.410
If Form, Truth, and Regret are
not present, it cannot be unsheathed.

20:30.290 --> 20:33.920
The intertwined fates of men give the Mononoke its Form,

20:33.920 --> 20:36.710
Truth is the natural state of all things,

20:36.710 --> 20:40.460
and Regret is ever-present in men’s hearts.

20:40.460 --> 20:42.840
And so, I’ll ask you all

20:50.100 --> 20:52.270
to tell me

20:53.690 --> 20:56.690
the Truth and Regret!

21:07.530 --> 21:09.950
To be continued

21:11.750 --> 21:19.250
Without you, I just can’t smile.

21:20.380 --> 21:30.310
I walk this banal town,

21:30.310 --> 21:36.390
feeling such intense emotions.

21:36.940 --> 21:42.780
I know that if I could treasure them and live on,

21:42.860 --> 21:52.080
I would need nothing else.

21:52.740 --> 22:00.250
The summer flowers that bloomed in the sky

22:00.250 --> 22:06.550
Come falling down, dancing in the wind.

22:06.630 --> 22:09.890
I can barely recall the night sky

22:09.890 --> 22:13.180
where they all came tumbling down,

22:13.180 --> 22:24.030
so what I can still recall is all the more precious.
